4.The figures for the quarter ended December 31, 2025 is derived / balancing figrure between audited figures in respect of the full financial year and the published unaudited year-to-date figures up to the third quarter of the financial year. &lt;BR&gt; 
5.The Board of Directors of Company at their meeting held on February 19, 2026 recommended final dividend of INR 7.00 per Equity Share of INR 10 each fully paid up for finacial year ending December 31, 2025. &lt;BR&gt; 
6.On 21 November 2025, the Government of India notified four Labour Codes consolidating 29 existing labour laws. The Company has assessed and disclosed the incremental impact of these changes on the basis of the best information available. Accordingly, the Company has recorded an incremental net impact on gratuity and long-term compensated absences of Rs. 103.57 million in the Standalone Statement of Profit and Loss for the quarter and year ended 31 December 2025. The Company continues to monitor the finalisation of Central/ State Rules and clarifications from the Government on other aspects of the Labour Code and would provide appropriate accounting effect on the basis of such developments as needed. &lt;BR&gt; 
